-- Gathering 5 in the storybook voice (Fake Guru, 16 Oct: "Proceed"), generated by scripts/gen-gathering-sql.ts 5 from the updated episode file.
-- Gathering 5, generated by scripts/gen-gathering-sql.ts. Do not edit by hand.
insert into public.gathering_scripts (series_id, season_number, week, data) values
('dark-moon', 1, 5, '{"meta":{"dc":11,"ueDc":9,"def":26,"atk":19,"reward":1030,"enemy":"The Hollowed","condition":"The hollowed: the first time an enemy is put down, it rises with 2 HP and loses its next strike.","ueAttr":"Charm","ueTitle":"THE ROLL-CALL","barWay":"The Roll-Call","barRisk":"Their Trust"},"steps":[{"t":"tonight","text":"Tonight: the Gathering. Into the wall, to the room they never found. Tonight calls on Charm.","section":""},{"t":"section","title":"Arrival","section":"Arrival"},{"t":"say","text":"Night in Highwall. No lamp burns anywhere in the dead city but one: the Order''s fire, high on the hill below his hall. There is no sound at all but your own breath.\n\nAcross the city, on its hill, stands his hall. Doors shut. Sealed with something older than locks.\n\nThe map ends a stone''s throw from the herald''s gate: a room hidden in the thickness of the old wall, one slit of a window facing the hall. The Order has kept its own watch on those same doors for centuries, from just up the hill, and never known the room was there.\n\nAt the foot of the wall you light your lamps to find the Seekers'' door. Up on the hill, the Order''s watchmen see the light moving. They do not see the room. They never have.","section":"Arrival"},{"t":"section","title":"The Approach","section":"The Approach"},{"t":"pick","vote":true,"question":"WHERE DO YOU MEET THEM?","options":[{"label":"THE GATE-TOWER DOOR","desc":"they can come at you only one at a time, and you have nowhere to go."},{"label":"THE STREET","desc":"under the herald''s gate. Room for you, and room for them."}],"section":"The Approach","mode":"vote"},{"t":"say","text":"You have as long to decide as it takes them to come down a hill. Wherever you stand, you meet them well short of the hidden room. Nobody leads them to that.","section":"The Approach"},{"t":"approach","title":"MAKE YOUR GROUND","ways":[{"by":"At the door","attr":"Might","verb":"drag a fallen lintel across the way"},{"by":"In the street","attr":"Intellect","verb":"read the street, and choose where to stand"}],"reward":"+500g · **and the party strikes first**","fail":"they are on you before you are set, and **they strike first**","section":"The Approach"},{"t":"say","text":"When they reach you, you are standing exactly where you meant to be, and they have to come to you.","cond":{"on":"approach","pass":true},"section":"The Approach"},{"t":"say","text":"The first of them is round the corner before you are set. You take the fight where it finds you, with your back to whatever stone is nearest.","cond":{"on":"approach","pass":false},"section":"The Approach"},{"t":"section","title":"The Battle","section":"The Battle"},{"t":"say","text":"The Order''s watchmen come down the hill fighting, and they are not alone. Something comes with them out of a side street: men in armour so old it has gone green and black, moving with a terrible steadiness. You cut one, and it does not bleed. You cut it again, and it does not stop. It keeps walking into your blade as if it had somewhere to be.","section":"The Battle"},{"t":"battle","name":"THE HOLLOWED","firstLines":["You strike first.","It strikes first."],"desc":"**It does not fall until it is broken:** put down, it gets up once more.","section":"The Battle"},{"t":"say","text":"When it is over, the armoured dead lie still at last, and the watchmen lie beside them, all but one.\n\nHe is sitting against the foot of the wall where he fell, one hand pressed to his side, a crumpled page in the other. He is not looking at you. He is looking up the hill, at the hall, and his lips are moving.\n\nKneel close enough and you can hear it. He is praying: the words of a page worn soft with saying.","section":"The Battle"},{"t":"section","title":"The United Effort","section":"The United Effort"},{"t":"say","text":"Up the hill, at the Order''s fire, there is a lantern that was not there before. The relief has come, and found the fire burning and nobody at it.\n\nA voice comes down the hill, unhurried.\n\n*\"Keep the dark.\"*\n\nAgainst the wall, the dying man lifts his head and answers it, as he has answered it every night of his life. *\"It keeps us.\"* It is hardly more than breath. It would not carry to the next house.\n\nThe voice on the hill waits. Then it calls again, a little to the left. It is calling the posts along the wall, one by one. Every man who should answer is lying in this street.\n\nSo you answer for them. One post, one voice. They have kept this watch together all their lives, and they know how each of them sounds. The wind is all that is on your side.","section":"The United Effort"},{"t":"ue","section":"The United Effort"},{"t":"say","text":"*\"Keep the dark.\"*","section":"The United Effort"},{"t":"ueEnd","won":true,"section":"The United Effort"},{"t":"say","text":"There is time, now.\n\nYou kneel beside him in the street. His eyes have not left the hall, and his lips have not stopped moving. Now it is quiet enough to hear the words.","cond":{"on":"ue","won":true},"section":"The United Effort"},{"t":"ueEnd","won":false,"section":"The United Effort"},{"t":"say","text":"There is no time. His eyes are still on the hall, but they no longer see it. The page comes gently out of his fist, and you are inside the wall before the first lantern reaches the gate.","cond":{"on":"ue","won":false},"section":"The United Effort"},{"t":"section","title":"The Verse of the Binding","section":"The Verse of the Binding"},{"t":"say","text":"*From the Third Book of the Order of the Dark Moon — The Verse of the Binding.*\n\n*Hear how they laid him down.*\n\n*They came to his doors in the night — his own, who had held his wall — and his doors were opened to them, because they were his own. They did not come with swords alone. They had found a way in old writings, older than his house, and whole where his house''s pages were not; they had gone out into the far places of the world and gathered the shards, and they carried them in their hands.*\n\n*He rose to meet them. He spoke each of their names. Not one of them answered him.*\n\n*Then there was light, and a blow — not the blow of a blade, but of his own gift, turned back upon him the way a river is turned back into its bed. And the king who would not kneel to the end of the world went down upon his knees, and then upon the floor; and his hand opened at his side, as a sleeper''s hand opens.*\n\n*They had not tried to kill him. They laid on him a sleep: the Undying Sleep, which holds him still.*\n\n*Those who had stood nearest him, when he fell, stood on. They keep his watch to this day.*\n\n*The fifth they did not scatter with the others. They kept it near him, under their own eyes. Of the fifth, the old words say only this:*","section":"The Verse of the Binding"},{"t":"say","text":"*Here the hand changes. One line is set apart, in the older hand:*","cond":{"on":"ue","won":false},"section":"The Verse of the Binding"},{"t":"say","text":"**\"The fifth drinks deep of moon-blood, and of no other.\"**\n\n*Until the throne rise whole.*","section":"The Verse of the Binding"},{"t":"say","text":"On *Until the throne rise whole*, his voice stops, and does not start again.","cond":{"on":"ue","won":true},"section":"The Verse of the Binding"},{"t":"say","text":"His page is the prayer, word for word, and one line on it is set apart in the older hand: *The fifth drinks deep of moon-blood, and of no other.* Folded behind it is a second, shorter page. It can wait.","section":"The Verse of the Binding"},{"t":"section","title":"Notice","section":"Notice"},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":"The one you fought did not bleed, and did not weigh what a man weighs. Under that armour there is very little left.","Agility":"None of the armoured ones came down the hill. They came out of the side street, where they have stood all week.","Intellect":"The watchman''s page is worn through at its folds. He did not need to read it.","Charm":"He died looking at the hall, and not at any of you. Whatever is in there, he was not afraid of it.","Craft":"Every strap on that armour was mended once, long ago, and never since. Nobody has tended these men in centuries.","Aim":"Up the hill the Order''s fire is still burning, and nobody is standing at it. Every watchman they had came down.","floor":"From the cobbles you watched one of the armoured ones walk past you without a glance. Its helm was turned to the hall the whole way."},"section":"Notice"},{"t":"act","label":"LOOK CLOSER","section":"Notice"},{"t":"lookCloser","lines":{"Might":"The cut you gave it is dry all the way in.","Agility":"Their footprints in the dust begin in the middle of the street. Before tonight they had not taken a step.","Intellect":"It is copied out in a child''s round hand. He has carried it since he was a boy.","Charm":"At the end, his face was glad.","Craft":"The buckles were fastened once and never undone.","Aim":"The chalk lies ready under their board, and tonight''s stroke has not been struck. The men who should have struck it came down the hill to you."},"section":"Notice"},{"t":"section","title":"The hidden room","section":"The hidden room"},{"t":"say","text":"The way into the hidden room is a stone''s throw away, and it is Seeker work.","section":"The hidden room"},{"t":"act","label":"OPEN IT","section":"The hidden room"},{"t":"say","text":"It opens under {TAPPER}''s hand. Inside, in a plain stone niche facing the window, lies the fifth. Nobody searched for it. The trail brought you straight to it, the way it was always meant to.\n\nIt is not the shape on the rubbing. It is smaller, and colder, and it does not feel like earth or wind or water or fire. It feels like holding a piece of the night between the stars. It is the first Stone any of you has ever held in your own hands.","section":"The hidden room"},{"t":"match","question":"WHICH OF YOUR FRAGMENTS IS THIS?","quote":"*\"Those who had stood nearest him, when he fell, stood on.\"*","source":"From the house wall at the end of the soldiers'' street","section":"The hidden room","answer":"5-4"},{"t":"say","text":"Tonight they were moving.","section":"The hidden room"},{"t":"match","question":"WHICH OF YOUR FRAGMENTS IS THIS?","quote":"*\"They kept it near him, under their own eyes.\"*","source":"From the broken fountain below the hall","cond":{"on":"ue","won":true},"section":"The hidden room","answer":"5-5"},{"t":"say","text":"You are standing in the room they kept it in. Its one window faces his hall.","section":"The hidden room"},{"t":"section","title":"The attempt","section":"The attempt"},{"t":"say","text":"The older hand, on the watchman''s page: *The fifth drinks deep of moon-blood, and of no other.*","section":"The attempt"},{"t":"say","text":"Meira''s margin, from the drowned market cross: *\"''Moon-blood'' — the old songs'' word for the marked.\"*","section":"The attempt"},{"t":"say","text":"Garrick says nothing. He''s watching the Stone.\n\nA knife goes round the room, hilt first.","section":"The attempt"},{"t":"act","label":"OPEN YOUR PALM","section":"The attempt"},{"t":"say","text":"Nothing.\n\nNot a flicker. Not a warmth. The Stone lies in your hands as cold and dark as it was when you found it, and your blood runs off it like rain off glass.\n\nGarrick binds each cut palm himself, without being asked, in the same neat white linen you''ve seen on every child you''ve saved. Nobody remarks on it. There''s nothing strange about a man having linen to spare.","section":"The attempt"},{"t":"section","title":"The turn","section":"The turn"},{"t":"say","text":"For a long moment nobody can speak.","section":"The turn"},{"t":"turn","question":"*What did the Seekers'' last fragment say?*","section":"The turn","nudge":"*It is in your Chest.*","answer":"*\"Where he fell, under the dark moon, the five were joined.\"*\n\nNot here. Not now.\n\nGarrick is looking not at the Stone but out of the window, at the hall on the hill. *\"The old telling names a place, and a night.\"*"},{"t":"section","title":"The Watch","section":"The Watch"},{"t":"say","text":"The second page from the watchman''s fist is shorter, and older, and it is the one that makes the room go cold.","section":"The Watch"},{"t":"say","text":"*From the Third Book of the Order of the Dark Moon — The Watch.*\n\n*Hear, you who are faithful. Keep the watch where he fell. Keep his hall in sight, and let no night pass uncounted.*\n\n*The sleep is thinnest when the moon goes dark. On that night of all nights, he hears. On that night of all nights, the faithful gather where he fell, and do not leave him to wake alone.*\n\n*Count the nights.*\n\n*Until the throne rise whole.*","section":"The Watch"},{"t":"say","text":"Beneath it, in a living hand, is a watch-tally: a stroke crossed out for every night, down to the last few left. Seven.\n\nThe page goes with you.","section":"The Watch"},{"t":"section","title":"The Cliffhanger","section":"The Cliffhanger"},{"t":"say","text":"Seven strokes left on the tally. Seven nights.\n\nThe fifth lies in your cut palms and stays cold. Garrick has bound every one of them in his white linen. He does not tell you it will be all right.\n\nYou look out through the slit at the hall. The doors are shut, as they have been for centuries, sealed in a way no hand you know of can open. And somewhere inside, slow and heavy, you can hear it again: the heartbeat that first came to you from the north. It is not far away any more.\n\nAbove the hall, framed in the slit, the moon hangs at the half: seven nights from full, seven nights from swallowed whole.\n\nGarrick looks at the moon a long moment. *\"We''re early.\"*\n\nThen, across the square below the hall, a new lantern comes out of the dark. A watchman, a fresh one, takes up the chalk and draws it through tonight''s stroke, late. Now the board and the page agree: seven left.\n\nHe turns, lantern raised, and looks straight down the hill at the wall. At the slit window you are standing behind.","section":"The Cliffhanger"},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE WALL AT HIGHWALL** · Gathering 5","{EARNED}","The party: Battle {battle} · the roll-call {ue:answered|lost} · the watchman''s prayer {ue:said|read}","You learned: **the Seekers did not kill him. They turned his own gift on him, and he sleeps.** His soldiers still stand his watch, and tonight they walked. You hold the fifth, the first Stone you have ever held. Your blood did nothing to it. The Seekers say why: *where he fell, under the dark moon.* The Order is counting to that night. Seven.","You hold: **the fifth** · **the watch-page**","Tomorrow: **a watchman, looking straight at your window**"],"section":"The Cliffhanger"}],"ue":{"success":{"0":["The last post answers. On the hill, the lantern is set down beside the fire. Somebody sits."],"1":["Somebody up there laughs at something, low. It is not at you.","The calls are coming quicker. They want to be done, and sitting down."],"2":["You let the wind take half of it. That is how a man answers who has said it ten thousand times.","By now you have the cadence of it. The watch barely waits for you to finish."],"3":["You give it the way he gave it: flat, and a little bored. Up the hill, a lantern that had lifted comes down again.","The answer goes up into the dark. A voice comes back with the next call, in no hurry."]},"fail":{"0":["A third lantern, and a fourth. They start down the hill."],"1":["Two of them are talking now, low, and not calling anyone.","A second lantern is lit from the first."],"2":["The words are right, and the voice is wrong. Up at the fire, somebody stands.","The call comes again for the same post. They did not like the first answer."],"3":["A breath too quick. On the hill a lantern lifts, and hangs there, and is slow to come down.","Too loud. A man on a wall at night does not answer like a man who wants to be heard. Nobody calls the next post for a long moment."]},"between":["Against the wall, his lips are still moving.","The wind is off the hill. It carries every word down to you, and yours up.","In the side street, something in armour shifts, and is still."]}}'::jsonb)
on conflict (series_id, season_number, week) do update set data = excluded.data;
